Usage: id [OPTION]... [USER]

Print user and group information for the specified USER,
or (when USER omitted) for the current user.

Note: This is a Windows implementation. Windows doesn't have
POSIX UIDs/GIDs, so this command provides limited functionality.
It mainly displays the username.

OPTIONS:
  -a             ignore, for compatibility with other versions
  -g, --group    print only the effective group ID
  -G, --groups   print all group IDs
  -n, --name     print a name instead of a number
  -r, --real     print the real ID instead of the effective ID
  -u, --user     print only the effective user ID
  -Z, --context  print only the security context (not implemented)
      --zero     delimit entries with NUL, not whitespace
  -z             delimit entries with NUL, not whitespace
      --help     display this help and exit
  -V, --version  output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
